    "updated_at": "2017-10-18T22:06:05Z",
    "body": "Thank you for the quick response! \r\n\r\nI took a look at the **time marches on** steps again and there are a few things that are unclear to me that maybe you could help clarify:\r\n\r\n- There is mention of \"while the media element's show poster flag is not set\" in the description of when **time marches on** should be run. Could you clarify what the show poster flag is intended to be an indication of?\r\n- What should the active flag for a text track cue that has just been added to a text track be set to? \r\n- Is the expected behavior that the `cuechange` event happens before the video starts playing if there is a text track cue with a start time at 0?\r\n- Is it expected behavior for the `cuechange` event to accompany the `ended` event if there is a text track cue with a start time at the duration of the video?",
